## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests understanding of three-valued propagation on monotone constraints and the ability to design minimal backtracking strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Three-valued logic with ordering T > U > F
- Edge-wise monotone constraints on a directed graph
- Fixed-point propagation with backtracking for conflict resolution

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(nodes, edges, init) {
  const rank = { 'T': 2, 'U': 1, 'F': 0 };
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [from, to] of edges) {
      if (rank[nodes[to]] < rank[nodes[from]]) {
        nodes[to] = nodes[from];
        changed = true;
      }
    }
  }
  return nodes;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical logical deduction and simple SAT handling in a controlled, small-domain setting.

## Key Concepts
- Implication with negation
- Disjunction
- Satisfiability search
- Backtracking basics
- Early termination on first valid assignment

## Code Example
```javascript
function isSat(A,B) {
  // Clause1: (!A => B)  == (A || B)
  // Clause2: (B => A)   == (!B || A)
  // Clause3: (A || B)
  return (A || B) && (!B || A) && (A || B);
}
```

